    "body": "Triage, checked on `main` 8f30bee. Agreed that this is too big for one issue. Here's what exists today and a split.\n\n**What Post has now**\n- The dialog is a plain save-file picker: always `program.nc`, no starting folder (`state.rs::post_program_dialog`), so nothing is remembered between posts or taken from the project's name.\n- The program number is hard-coded `O0001`, followed by the machine name as a comment (`fanuc.cps`, `mazak.cps`, `fanuc-lathe.cps`).\n- The only user option is the Fanuc Lathe's threading choice (`schema::PostOptions`, #34), drawn under the post picker. The scripts read a handful of `properties` (`Compensation`, `CompensationType`, `FeedRate`, `SpindleSpeed`), and those come from the operations, not from the user.\n- The machine (and with it rigid tapping, belt ranges and coolant codes, #170) is a per-document choice through the Machine door. The verification gate judges the program against that machine's limits.\n\n**Suggested split** (each its own issue):\n1. **Output file:** start in the last post's folder (or the project's), and name the file after the project. Small, UI only. I can take this one.\n2. **Program number and comment:** a document field the posts write instead of `O0001`, per dialect (O-number, Heidenhain program name, Sinumerik `%_N_..._MPF`).\n3. **Per-post properties:** generalise `PostOptions` from the one threading field into a list each `.cps` declares (name, type, default), shown under the picker and saved in the document. Then optional stop, sequence numbers, `M6` on or off, the tool-list header, and dwell units become a post's own declared properties, not hard-coded fields.\n4. **Safe retract** (`G28` / `G30` / clearance plane) and **tapping style** (rigid / standard / self-reversing): the machine already carries `rigid_tapping` (#170), so these probably belong in the `.mch` with the post reading them.\n5. **Machine and units override at post time:** I'd suggest dropping these. The gate judges the program against the document's machine, so swapping the machine only at post time would post a program nothing judged for that machine. Changing the document's machine already re-judges.\n6. **Coolant extras and the chip conveyor** (multi-coolant, SmartCool, washdown): machine-specific M-codes, which fit the `.mch` coolant list (#150, #170) more than a dialog.\n\n**Clean-room note:** the option list reads like a commercial post's property sheet. The properties should come from the controllers' own programming manuals (as #170's machine files come from Tormach's manuals), not from a vendor post's property names or behaviour.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
